---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Projects"
description: "Explore web development case studies, platform migrations, and technical implementations by Abhishek Dahal."
permalink: "/projects/"
---

<div class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-header">
      <h1>All Projects & Case Studies</h1>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        A collection of web development implementations, CMS builds, and technical digital projects.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="projects-grid">
      {% for project in collections.projects %}
        {% include "components/project-card.njk" %}
      {% else %}
        <p style="grid-column: 1 / -1; color: var(--text-muted); font-style: italic;">
          No projects found in the collection. Add Markdown files in <code>src/projects/</code>.
        </p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 4rem; padding: 2rem; background-color: var(--bg-surface); border: 1px dashed var(--border-color); border-radius: var(--radius-md);">
      <h3 style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem;">💡 About the sample projects above</h3>
      <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 0;">
        The projects shown here are clearly marked placeholder demonstrations to illustrate the responsive grid, optional fields (such as confidential flags, live links, and repository links), and detail case study layouts. You can replace them with your real projects simply by editing or adding Markdown files in <code>src/projects/</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
